        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.644,
            0.05,
            0.846,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Operations with Integers"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.089,
            0.577,
            0.184
          ],
          "content": "Even when the multiplier is negative, the same pattern is observed. When the multiplicand is negative, for every unit **decrease** in the multiplier, the product **increases** by the multiplicand."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.594,
            0.089,
            0.726,
            0.107
          ],
          "content": "4 \\times ( - 3) = - 12",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.594,
            0.117,
            0.715,
            0.136
          ],
          "content": "3 \\times ( - 3 ) = - 9",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.594,
            0.145,
            0.714,
            0.165
          ],
          "content": "2 \\times ( - 3 ) = - 6",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.184,
            0.577,
            0.261
          ],
          "content": "We can see from these patterns that, what is true for multiplication when the integers are positive, is also true when the integers are negative."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.595,
            0.175,
            0.714,
            0.194
          ],
          "content": "1 \\times ( - 3 ) = - 3",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.594,
            0.203,
            0.704,
            0.221
          ],
          "content": "0 \\times ( - 3 ) = 0",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.595,
            0.231,
            0.727,
            0.252
          ],
          "content": "(-1) \\times (-3) = 3",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.594,
            0.259,
            0.726,
            0.282
          ],
          "content": "(-2) \\times (-3) = 6",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.594,
            0.289,
            0.728,
            0.309
          ],
          "content": "(-3) \\times (-3) = 9",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.324,
            0.847,
            0.383
          ],
          "content": "With this understanding of multiplication of integers, let us look at the times 3 tables when the multipliers and multiplicands are positive, and when they are negative."
